    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster as our premier start (83.29). His matchup against a right-handed arm with an xERA of 4.41 is highly favorable, and with a significant +14% dynamic platoon boost and a prime #3 spot in the order, he is positioned for an elite performance. Following him, **Drake Baldwin** (72.67) and **Jackson Merrill** (71.40) offer the highest floors among our non-core stars. **Drake Baldwin** benefits immensely from a park factor surge (+16%) while hitting leadoff, and **Jackson Merrill** provides a stable secondary source of production against a softer matchup facing a 4.58 xERA starter. \n\nWe are leaning heavily into platoon advantages today, most notably with **Denzer Guzman**, whose score of 53.14 is bolstered by a massive +19% SP skill adjustment and a helpful wind direction. Conversely, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (48.16) and **Nasim Nunez** (54.30) face tougher individual tests against a left-handed arm, dragging their totals down despite their secondary utility. Our most difficult decision on the bench was **Jorge Polanco** (45.78); he was the final cut, narrowly missing the lineup due to a negative park factor adjustment and a poor matchup against a 3.67 xERA pitcher that made him less efficient than our current middle infield options. \n\nThe lineup carries moderate risk, particularly regarding the weather and pitcher skill profiles. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains a strong play at 66.25, his score is actively suppressed by a -5% wind-in penalty, necessitating a cautious outlook for power metrics. Additionally, we are monitoring **Heliot Ramos** (56.33), who faces a potential threat from the opposing catcher's elite pop-time, which could stifle our pursuit of stolen bases\u2014a critical category for our team strategy. We will continue to track final lineup confirmations to ensure these projections hold throughout the afternoon.",
